WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:04.930
Oberon is the outermost and second-largest major moon of the planet Uranus.

00:05.377 --> 00:11.062
It is the second-most massive of the Uranian moons, and the tenth-largest moon in the Solar System.

00:11.633 --> 00:22.838
Discovered by William Herschel in 1787, Oberon is named after the mythical king of the fairies who appears as a character in Shakespeare's A Midsummer Night's Dream.

00:23.438 --> 00:27.218
Its orbit lies partially outside Uranus's magnetosphere.
